## Phase 2: Markdown Parsing

### 2.1: TODO Item Model
**Priority:** MUST  
**Estimated Effort:** 3 hours  
**Dependencies:** 1.5  
**Files:** `internal/todo/item.go`, `internal/todo/item_test.go`

- [ ] Create `internal/todo` package
- [ ] Define `Item` struct
  - `Description string`
  - `Done bool`
  - `IsFIXME bool`
  - `LineNumber int`
  - `Project *project.Project`
- [ ] Implement `Parse(line string) (*Item, error)`
  - Detect checkbox: `- [ ]`, `* [ ]`, `+ [ ]`
  - Detect done state: `[x]`, `[X]`
  - Extract description
  - Detect FIXME prefix (case-insensitive)
  - Return nil for non-TODO lines
- [ ] Implement `(i *Item) String() string`
  - Format as markdown: `- [ ] description`
  - Use `[X]` for done items
- [ ] Write unit tests
  - Test all checkbox variations
  - Test FIXME detection
  - Test round-trip (Parse → String → Parse)
  - Test malformed input

**Acceptance Criteria:**
- Parses all TODO formats
- FIXME detection works
- Round-trip preserves semantics
- Test coverage ≥ 90%

---

### 2.2: Markdown Section Parser
**Priority:** MUST  
**Estimated Effort:** 4 hours  
**Dependencies:** 2.1  
**Files:** `internal/parser/section.go`, `internal/parser/section_test.go`

- [ ] Create `internal/parser` package
- [ ] Define `SectionType` enum
  - `SectionHeader`
  - `SectionTODO`
  - `SectionOther`
- [ ] Define `Section` struct
  - `Type SectionType`
  - `Content string`
  - `Line int`
  - `Project *project.Project`
- [ ] Implement `SplitSections(content string) []Section`
  - Split markdown by headers and TODO blocks
  - Detect header level (`#`, `##`, etc.)
  - Preserve exact whitespace
  - Track line numbers
- [ ] Write unit tests
  - Test simple markdown
  - Test nested headers
  - Test mixed content
  - Test whitespace preservation

**Acceptance Criteria:**
- Splits markdown correctly
- Preserves all formatting
- Accurate header level detection
- Test coverage ≥ 85%

---

### 2.3: Markdown Document Parser
**Priority:** MUST  
**Estimated Effort:** 6 hours  
**Dependencies:** 2.2  
**Files:** `internal/parser/markdown.go`, `internal/parser/markdown_test.go`

- [ ] Define `Document` struct
  - `FilePath string`
  - `Sections []Section`
  - `Projects map[string]*project.Project`
- [ ] Implement `Parse(filePath string, projects map[string]*project.Project) (*Document, error)`
  - Read markdown file
  - Split into sections using `SplitSections`
  - Match header titles to project titles
  - Extract TODO items from matched sections
  - Populate project.Items
  - Preserve all non-TODO content
- [ ] Implement `(d *Document) FindProject(name string) (*project.Project, error)`
- [ ] Create test fixtures in `testdata/markdown/`
  - `simple.md` - Basic TODO list
  - `nested.md` - Nested projects
  - `mixed.md` - TODO and non-TODO content
  - `complex.md` - Real-world example
- [ ] Write comprehensive tests

**Acceptance Criteria:**
- Parses complex markdown
- All non-TODO content preserved exactly
- Headers matched to projects
- TODO items extracted with line numbers
- Test coverage ≥ 85%

---

### 2.4: Markdown Writer
**Priority:** MUST  
**Estimated Effort:** 5 hours  
**Dependencies:** 2.3  
**Files:** `internal/parser/writer.go`, `internal/parser/writer_test.go`

- [ ] Implement `(d *Document) Write(filePath string) error`
  - Reconstruct markdown from sections
  - Update TODO sections with modified items
  - Preserve all formatting
  - Use atomic write pattern:
    1. Write to temp file
    2. Sync temp file
    3. Rename to target (atomic)
  - Preserve file permissions
  - Preserve line endings (detect LF vs CRLF)
- [ ] Handle errors gracefully
  - Clean up temp files on error
  - Return clear error messages
- [ ] Write tests
  - Test round-trip (Parse → Write → Parse)
  - Test permission preservation
  - Test atomic write (simulate failure)
  - Test line ending preservation

**Acceptance Criteria:**
- Atomic writes (no data loss)
- Permissions preserved
- Line endings preserved
- Round-trip test passes
- Test coverage ≥ 80%

